"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Lunar Force","oracle_id":"31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799","oracle_text":"When an opponent casts a spell, sacrifice this enchantment and counter that spell.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-07-22","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Playing a land is not casting a spell, so playing a land will not trigger this card.","oracle_id":"11eb31d9-cbcb-4ec5-abab-dfa646addbba","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The spell will be countered even if Lunar Force can’t be sacrificed, most likely because it has already left the battlefield. Casting a spell in response to an opponent’s Lunar Force’s triggered ability is generally a bad idea.","oracle_id":"31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799","published_at":"2016-07-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can’t choose not to sacrifice Lunar Force.","oracle_id":"31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799","published_at":"2016-07-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You sacrifice Lunar Force even if the spell’s already been countered, perhaps by the ability of another Lunar Force, or if the spell can’t be countered.","oracle_id":"31b18e10-c74d-4384-a0e2-def0b3ec4799","published_at":"2016-07-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura’s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn’t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent’s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura’s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can’t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it’s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
